{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>From distress [מעצר], etc.</b> Now HaShem is the redeemer of Israel, and the truth is [the lot of] the righteous of Israel." "<b>Taken [לוקח].</b> HaShem took him from distress, and he was distressed." "<b>And from judgment [וממשפט].</b> Judgment of vengeance." "<b>And his generation, who will recount [ואת דורו מי ישוחח].</b> Like \"or speak to the earth and it will instruct you\" (Job 12:8), and the meaning is: who would have told the people of his generation that it would be so, when he was already as one cut off from the land of the living." "<b>For the transgression of my people [מפשע עמי].</b> My words are for every nation, and this is that the affliction that would come upon Israel was because of our transgressions, like \"wounded for our transgressions.\" The correct view is that it is so: because of the transgression of my people the affliction would come upon them, on account of the word למו, which is like \"to them.\""], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 53, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:22.574209527Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}